==Trivia== 
*The card's name is a reference to Nikola Tesla, a famous scientist known for working with electricity. It is based on one of his inventions, the Tesla coil which wirelessly transmits electricity to the destination; the way tesla coil transmits electricity appears similar to how the Tesla attacks. 
**In the Spanish, Korean, Chinese, and Vietnamese language settings of the game, the Tesla's name translates to "Tesla Tower", "Thunderbolt Tower", "Tesla Electromagnetic Tower", and "Electric Arc Tower" respectively.
*Electricity was first detected through electric fish from as far back as 2750 BCE where Ancient Egyptian texts described them as the "protectors" of all other fish. At around 600 BCE, Thales of Miletus made a series of observations on static electricity, from which he believed that friction rendered amber magnetic, in contrast to minerals such as magnetite, which needed no rubbing. Thales was incorrect in believing the attraction was due to a magnetic effect, but later science would prove a link between magnetism and electricity. Electricity would remain little more than an intellectual curiosity for millennia until 1600, when the English scientist William Gilbert wrote ''De Magnete'', in which he made a careful study of electricity and magnetism, distinguishing the lodestone effect from static electricity produced by rubbing amber.
**The Tesla is 1 of 3 evolved [[cards]] associated with electricity, with the others being [[Zap/Evolution|Zap]] and [[Electro Dragon/Evolution|Electro Dragon]].
***Despite both the attacks and pulses being composed of electricity, only the Evolved Tesla’s pulses can stun troops.
*Among all evolved [[:Category:Building Cards|buildings]] that can attack, the Evolved Tesla is tied with [[Cannon/Evolution|Cannon]] for the shortest range of all buildings, with a range of 5.5 tiles.
*Like many other Evolutions, the Evolved Tesla plays an unique sound effect when deployed. However, due to a glitch, when deployed by the opponent, the [[Mortar/Evolution|Evolved Mortar]]'s deployment sound is played at the same time.
*The Tesla is unavailable in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]]. More specifically:
**It is 1 of 20 cards that is unavailable in [[Mirror]] mode, the others being [[Minions]], [[Cannon]], [[Mortar]], [[Goblin Hut]], [[Tombstone]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Inferno Tower]], [[Barbarian Hut]], [[Furnace]], [[Elixir Collector]], [[Freeze]], [[Clone]], [[X-Bow]], [[Golden Knight]], [[Skeleton King]], [[Archer Queen]], [[Mighty Miner]], [[Little Prince]], and the [[Monk]].
**It is unavailable in [[Global Spell|The Floor is Healing]] sub-[[:Category:Modes|mode]] of the Global Spell game mode, much like other building cards, as well as the [[Cannon Cart]].
*The Tesla's Evolution is the subject of an [[Emotes|Emote]].

